# Mobile (iOS and Android)

Rules shared by both phones. Platform specifics: {{MOBILE_PLATFORM_LINKS}}.

## Theme

`make tokens` writes the theme files under `assets/platforms/mobile/` (`{{THEME_NAME}}Theme.swift`, `{{THEME_NAME}}Theme.kt`,
for the platforms this project chose). Copy them into the app (or point the app at them); never edit them by hand, and
never write raw colours, sizes or durations in screens. Dark mode follows the system appearance.

## Touch and layout

- Touch targets at least 44pt (iOS) and 48dp (Android), even when the drawing is smaller.
- Respect safe areas, the keyboard and the home indicator; primary actions stay reachable with one thumb.
- Design for the smallest supported phone first, then larger phones and tablets.

## Navigation

Tab bar or bottom navigation for top-level places (3 to 5); a stack for depth; sheets for focused tasks. Back is always
available and predictable. The product's navigation model is in [../ux.md](../ux.md).

## Type and text

Use the generated text styles; they scale with the system font size (Dynamic Type on iOS, font scale on Android). Check the
largest sizes.

## Feedback

Haptics only for confirmation or errors the user caused; pressed state on every tappable item; loading shows a skeleton or
progress, never a frozen screen.

## First screens

Build in this order: app shell and navigation, the main list or home, the main detail, the main form, then settings.
